## Intent classifier (template era)

`classifyIntent()` in `lib/agent/inboundDraft.ts` — regex on subject + excerpt. **Order is the contract** (do not reshuffle without tests):

| Priority | intentHint | Triggers (summary) |
|---------:|------------|-------------------|
| 1 | `payment_dispute` | refund, chargeback, dispute, … (wins even if sticker words present) |
| 2 | `shipping` | ship, tracking, delivery, *where is my* (wins even if sticker words present) |
| 3 | `bespoke_product` | bespoke, custom, logo, label(s), sticker(s), print/printing, decal, vinyl, iron-on, name tags |
| 4 | `fundraising` | fundrais, partner, commission, payout, P&C — **not** bare “school” |
| 5 | `order_status` | order, receipt (only if no product-enquiry words) |
| 6 | `general` | default |

**Print/sticker Contact enquiries (Rachele class — closed 2026-09):** *print large stickers for a billy kart* → `bespoke_product` + size/qty/artwork ask. Cousins covered in `inboundDraft.test.ts`: school-bag labels ≠ fundraising; “I ordered custom stickers” ≠ generic order_status.

**Payment disputes:** special opening + “do not share full card numbers” line — keep for compliance tone.

