## Queue filters vs deep-link

Shared helpers live in `lib/agent/inboundQueue.ts` (`INBOUND_*_ACTIONABLE_STATUSES`, `INBOUND_*_RECENT_STATUSES`, `include*InRecentQueue`).

| Source | Included statuses |
|--------|-------------------|
| **Needs attention** tab | message: `new`, `read` — bespoke: `new`, `reviewed` |
| **Recently handled** tab | message: `replied`, `closed` — bespoke: `replied`, `approved`, `rejected` (newest 40) |
| Deep-link `?channel=&id=` | **Any** status — pin on Needs attention, `deepLinkOnly: true` if outside actionable statuses |

Do not regress: Messages/Bespoke **Draft with Agent** must always load that row’s excerpt on the draft screen.

**Cousins / edge cases (keep covered):**

- Empty Needs attention + non-empty Recent → empty copy must offer “View N recently handled”
- Both empty → Messages / Bespoke links + Draft with Agent hint
- Send → status `replied` → item leaves Needs attention and appears under Recently handled
- Hub `newMessages`/`newBespoke` = 0 while Needs attention still has `read`/`reviewed` rows (stats ≠ tab count)
- Multi-admin: another admin marks replied → Refresh queue; no live WS required for Wave 3

